// Go workspace for the Optimiq Voice data plane (plan §3.3: "Go apps live in a go.work workspace;
// single repo, per-app go.mod, CI parity with turbo").
//
// TypeScript remains the default language; Go is used where the 2026 industry consensus is Go —
// the SIP edge and, later, the media plane. Everything here consumes the same NATS contract as the
// TypeScript services, via packages/events-go.
//
//	packages/events-go   generated + hand-written NATS contract (peer of @optimiq-voice/events)
//	apps/sipd            SIP edge: registrar today, proxy next; retires Routr in P6
//	apps/mediad          NOT YET — RTP/media plane on Pion; add its `use` line when it lands
//
//	go work sync && go build ./... && go test ./...
go 1.26

use (
	./apps/sipd
	./packages/events-go
)
